From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1156 redfin: CommCenter data-capable gate
 (kern.sweet_cc_datacap, default off)

Boot-arg/sysctl sweetccdatacap (int, default 0: nothing changes). When 1, in a
process named CommCenter, shared_region_check_np() patches one instruction in
CommCenter's MAIN executable: the data-capability stub vf438 (sub_1003cb48c,
file offset 0x3cb48c == unslid VA 0x1003cb48c) is flipped from mov w0,#0
(0x52800000, not data-capable) to mov w0,#1 (0x52800020, data-capable), so the
four stub data-personality subclasses report data-capable and the
ActivationStatus / DataSettings gate (sub_100b2e380 -> vf438) passes and
cellular data can activate.

Mechanism mirrors 1061's sweet_abp_dyld_hook (the proven userland code-patch
from the kernel: proc_selfname + copyin verify + cs_allow_invalid +
vm_map_protect VM_PROT_COPY private COW + copyout + r-x + cache sync + read-back
verify), but patches the MAIN executable instead of the shared cache. The main
Mach-O base comes from current_task()->mach_header_vm_address via a new accessor
sweet_current_task_main_macho() in osfmk/kern/task.c, because struct task is
opaque to BSD (MACH_KERNEL_PRIVATE). sysctl kern.sweet_cc_datacap (RW int,
root-writable). Refuses safely on any byte mismatch; idempotent. Default off ->
baseline is byte-for-byte identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvABzcjCeDywTuc6ppYmC
---
